# LF everywhere, checked in and checked out.
#
# This project ships a trap that says a CRLF shebang fails on Linux as
# "/system/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter" and reads as a broken script. Shipping
# CRLF from a repo that warns about CRLF would be the first thing a reviewer
# screenshots - and the CI matrix runs on Ubuntu, where it would actually break.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
